@trait {
  name: "@profiler",
  category: "analytics",
  description: "Multi-level runtime profiler with configurable sampling, threshold-based alerting, and structured output for downstream analysis pipelines. level selects what the profiler instruments: call_stack collects a sampled call-stack histogram for CPU-bound hotspot analysis; memory instruments heap allocations and garbage-collection cycles, emitting heap snapshots at each sample; gpu captures GPU frame timing per draw call and compute dispatch, exposing per-pass utilisation percentages; network records per-request latency, payload size, and queuing delay for all outbound fetch/XHR calls within the attached entity's scope; all instruments every available dimension simultaneously. sample_rate_hz is the sampling frequency in samples per second; higher rates increase overhead and fidelity — 100 Hz is suitable for interactive sessions, 10 Hz for long-running background captures. threshold_ms is the per-frame budget in milliseconds; any sampled interval that exceeds this value triggers on_threshold, carrying the violated frame duration and the active level, so automated regression monitors can fire without polling. auto_start begins profiling immediately on entity attach without requiring an explicit on_start event. output_format controls the shape of the data emitted by on_sample and on_complete: chrome_json produces a JSON trace compatible with Chrome DevTools Profiler and Perfetto; flamegraph produces a collapsed stacks format consumable by FlameGraph.pl and speedscope; holoscript emits a structured HoloScript event payload with typed fields (spanName, duration_ms, level, metadata) consumable by @telemetry and @analytics downstream handlers. on_sample fires at each sample tick, carrying the raw frame payload formatted per output_format. on_complete fires when profiling is stopped via on_stop, carrying the full aggregated trace, total_samples, duration_ms, and mean_frame_ms. on_threshold fires when any individual sample exceeds threshold_ms, carrying the exceeded duration and the current level for fast alerting pipelines. Pairs with @telemetry for metric fanout, @circuit_breaker for automatic instrumentation suspension under high load, and @alert for threshold-based notification escalation. Research: ProfilerTrait.ts — span-based CPU timing; SpatialProfilerTrait.ts, TelemetryTrait.ts — GPU and analytics integration.",
  props: {
    level: enum("call_stack" | "memory" | "gpu" | "network" | "all") = "call_stack",
    sample_rate_hz: number = 100,
    threshold_ms: number = 16,
    output_format: enum("chrome_json" | "flamegraph" | "holoscript") = "holoscript",
    auto_start: boolean = false
  },
  events: {
    attached: "profiler:attached",
    detached: "profiler:detached",
    on_sample: "profiler:sample",
    on_complete: "profiler:complete",
    on_threshold: "profiler:threshold",
    on_start: "profiler:start",
    on_stop: "profiler:stop",
    on_pause: "profiler:pause",
    on_resume: "profiler:resume",
    on_status: "profiler:status"
  },
  behaviors: ["@telemetry"]
}
